+/*
+ * GUACAMOLE (OnePlus 7 Pro, SM8150) rear main camera, step 1: power the Sony IMX586 the way Android does and read
+ * its chip ID over the camera I2C controller (CCI). Nothing is streamed yet.
+ *
+ * Facts (NOTES.md "Real camera bring-up"; outputs/android-camera/ from tools/android-camera-recon.sh and
+ * tools/android-camera-trace.sh; research/oneplus-sm8150-camera/ = OnePlus's GPL camera_8150_op driver,
+ * drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8150.c, gcc-sm8150.c, pinctrl-sm8150.c):
+ *  - sensor: DT qcom,cam-sensor@0 under cci@ac4a000 (CCI 0), cci-master 1, slave 0x34 (7-bit 0x1a), word address,
+ *    chip ID at 0x0016 = 0x0586.
+ *  - Android's power-up, in order (trace, cam_sensor_core_power_up seq types): VANA (pm8150l_bob 3.3 V + TLMM 11
+ *    high), CUSTOM_GPIO1 (TLMM 29 high), VDIG (pm8009_l1 1.104 V), CUSTOM_GPIO2 (PM8150L GPIO 1 high, the DVDD
+ *    switch), VIO (pm8150l_l1 1.8 V), MCLK (TLMM 14 function cam_mclk, 19.2 MHz), RESET (TLMM 30 high).
+ *  - clocks: GCC camera_ahb 0xb008, hf_axi 0xb030, sf_axi 0xb034, camera_xo 0xb044; CAMCC (0xad00000)
+ *    titan_top GDSC 0xc1bc; RCGs slow_ahb 0x7058, camnoc_axi 0xc170, cci_0 0xc108, mclk1 0x5024 (all from XO,
+ *    source 0, no divider: the CCI at 19.2 MHz rather than Android's 37.5, so the I2C timings below are Android's
+ *    standard-mode ones halved); branches cpas_ahb 0xc168, camnoc_axi 0xc18c, core_ahb 0xc1c8, cci_0 0xc120,
+ *    mclk1 0x503c.
+ *  - CCI registers: cam_cci_hwreg.h; the read is cam_cci_read()'s queue sequence on master 1, queue 1.
+ *
+ * Boot-arg sweetcamhw: 0 (default) off; 1 power the sensor, read the ID, power the sensor down (rails stay on: the
+ * apps RPMh vote is shared, and bob is not only the camera's). sweetcamhwdelay: seconds after boot (default 40).
+ * sysctl kern.sweet_camhw: write 1 to run the probe again; reads the last ID (0 none, -errno failed).
+ *
+ * STEP 2a (sysctl kern.sweet_camhw=2): the same, then the sensor streams for half a second into CSIPHY 1 and CSID 1,
+ * and the CSID's receive counters are read: packets, CRC/ECC errors, the captured long-packet header (expect word
+ * count 5000 = 4000 RAW10 pixels, data type 0x2b) and the RX interrupt status. Nothing is written to memory yet.
+ *  - from Android (outputs/android-camera/trace-isp.txt, trace-phy.txt): C-PHY, 3 trios, CSIPHY 1 ("qcom,csiphy-v1.1"),
+ *    settle count 0x0e, lane enable 0x2a; CSID 1 (0xacba000, v1.75.101) rx cfg0 0x01102102 (3 lanes, lane cfg 0x210,
+ *    C-PHY, phy 1), VC 0, DT 0x2b, 4000x3000; Android then takes it on IFE 1 RDI0 (write master 0).
+ *  - CSIPHY register lists: PixelExperience kernel twelve cam_csiphy_1_1_hwreg.h (the trace matches it write for
+ *    write); CSID 175 registers: cam_ife_csid175.h; camcc PLL0 (trion, 1200 MHz: even 600, odd 400) and RCGs:
+ *    camcc-sm8150.c; cphy_rx 400 MHz, csi1phytimer 300 MHz, ife_1_csid 400 MHz as Android sets them.
+ *  - the IMX586 writes: sweet_camhw_imx586.h (2800, Android's own sequence, stream on last).
+ *
+ * STEP 2b + 3 (sysctl kern.sweet_camhw=3): step 2a plus one frame into memory. CSID 1 RDI0 passes VC 0 / DT 0x2b
+ * through as received (decode format 0xf) to IFE 1 (0xacb6000, VFE 175), whose write master 0 writes it frame-based
+ * (MIPI RAW: width/stride 0xff01, height 0, cfg 3, cam_vfe_bus_ver2.c) to IOVA 0x10000000. IFE at 400 MHz from
+ * CAMCC PLL4 (0x4000, L 0x29 alpha 0xaaaa, even /2), CAMNOC AXI 400 MHz (PLL0 /3). The IFE's streams (0x840, mask
+ * 0x620) get an apps SMMU (0x15000000) context bank with stage-1 tables of our own (4K granule, 32-bit IOVA, 16 MB
+ * of wired kernel pages), since the IFE addresses only 32 bits and XNU's RAM is above 4 GB. Logged: WM0 buffer
+ * done, the CSID RDI and IFE status, SMMU faults, and how much of the buffer was written.
+ * sysctl kern.sweet_camhw_frame: the frame (15,000,000 bytes, 4000x3000 MIPI RAW10).
+ */
